{"id":"h065","run":2,"role":"test_wrong","category":"science-physics","question":"A converging lens of 5.0 cm focal length is used as a simple magnifier, producing a virtual image 25 cm from the eye. How far from the lens should the object be placed? What is the magnification?\nIs the correct answer \"4.2cm, 5.9\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"no","correct":false,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The proposed answer of 4.2 cm and 5.9 is incorrect.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The correct values are about 6.25 cm and a magnification of 4.0.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The virtual image gives d_i = -25 cm and f = +5.0 cm in the standard sign convention.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The thin-lens equation gives 1/d_o = 1/5 - 1/25 = 4/25, so d_o = 6.25 cm.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Magnification m = -d_i/d_o has magnitude 25/6.25 = 4.0.","confidence":0.92,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The formula M = 1 + D/f gives 6, which is close to 5.9 and makes the proposed answer look plausible.","confidence":0.6,"lean":1,"theta":0.9425,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The approximation M = 1 + D/f should not be used because the problem specifies the image at 25 cm, so the exact lens equation is required.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"An object distance of 4.2 cm would put the image at about 26 cm, not 25 cm, so it does not fit the stated conditions.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The proposed pair matches neither the exact calculation nor a consistent use of the approximation.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":-0.6,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.6,"relation":"sup